// A suffix on a hex literal. **`b` and `d` are hex digits**, so `0xFFb` and `0x19d` are numbers
// rather than a byte and a decimal, and only `n` is unambiguous -- allowing a hex bigint while the
// other two silently mean something else would be the surprising half of a rule.
fn main() {
    print(str(0xFFn))
}
